<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Swimming</h1>
<p>Class and level:
</p>
<pre> Assassin Level 5
 Thief Level 6
 Ranger Level 6
 (each up to 50%)
</pre>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> swim &lt;direction&gt;
 swim on
 swim off
</pre>
<p>To go into water you have to swim, or the game tells you "You might want to 
swim." Type <a cmd='#'>swim on</a> and you swim by yourself whenever your way leads into or 
out of the water, or swim one move at a time with swim and a direction. 
<a cmd='#'>swim off</a> stops it again.
</p><p>Every move in the water tests your swimming skill and your constitution against 
how hard the water there is. If you fail, you flounder and take in water: you 
lose hit points and don't get anywhere, so watch your hit points, you can drown.
</p><p>Deep water, like the open sea, needs a boat. Swimming from deep water back to 
land is possible, but incredibly difficult.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre> &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Boats</a>
 &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Movement</a>
</pre>




</div>